        "Re‑watch the 'Introduction to Data Structures' video, pausing at each definition slide and summarizing the term in your own words.",
        "Create a two‑column flashcard set: left column = term (instance, schema, object, class), right column = precise definition and a real‑world analogy.",
        "After each flashcard review, write a one‑sentence example that uses the term correctly.",
        "Complete the 10‑question “definition drill” quiz in the course app, reviewing explanations for every wrong answer before moving on."
