        "Read the 'Purpose of Data Structures' section of the notes, then write a 150‑word paragraph explaining why data structures are used, citing at least two concrete examples (e.g., searching, sorting).",
        "Map each data structure covered (array, linked list, stack, queue) to a real‑world problem where it provides a clear advantage.",
        "Complete the “Why Use a Data Structure?” worksheet, which asks you to match scenarios with the most appropriate structure and justify the choice."
